Thumper's loading screen intermittently killed the process (silent, no
crash report) when spawning worker threads. Bisected with ThreadInit step
markers over three runs: death inside the per-thread LookupCache ctor.
Each thread committed L2 (128MB, sized for 64GB VirtualMemSize) +
CODE_SIZE (128MB) + L1 upfront (iOS can't commit-on-fault) — ~264MB ×
~19 threads ≈ 5GB.

- Config.VirtualMemSize 64GB → 8GB on iOS (ContextImpl ctor): L2 shrinks
  128MB → 16MB. DLL code at ~0x7EExxxxxxxxx aliased in L2 even at 64GB
  and is served by the dispatcher's loop-top L1 probe; the exe at
  0x140000000 stays covered.
- CODE_SIZE 128MB → 64MB on iOS: overflow path is a clean
  ClearCodeCache (AllocateBackingForPage returns 0).
- ThreadInit step markers (Module.cpp TI:*, Core.cpp [TI-IC]) + alloc
  size/result logging kept for future thread-death forensics.

Verified: 20/20 threads init, loading no longer crashes, long stable
gameplay session.

